# Bran tells Serra about the door. Only reachable once she is traveling
# with the company (Act 5) and he chose to tell her.
#
# TIMING: this scene is Act 5 only - Serra does not travel with the company
# until then.
#
# {PLAYER} is whoever is standing there when he finally does it.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_BranSerra

== start ==
Bran waits until the fire is low and there are three of them left awake. It is as close to alone with her as he is going to get.

"Captain. Hesk did not die in the pass."

Serra puts down what she is holding.

* [Let him say it.] -> say
* "He has been carrying this a long time." -> say

== say ==
He says it plainly and in order, the way he does everything: the push, the ruin, the cellar, the four days, the hammering, the two days of it, the sword across his knees. The beam. Six strokes and a seventh half cut.

He does not soften the number. He gives her the number first.

* [Continue.] -> serra

== serra ==
Serra listens the whole way through without one interruption.

Then: "Six days."

"Yes."

"And you were up there for twelve."

"Yes."

* [Wait.] -> verdict

== verdict ==
She looks at the fire for a long moment.

"I put him in that pass," she says. "I took him on because he told the truth at hiring, and I sent him up the north side because he was the only one I could spare, and I did not go back for four days because I was counting the ones I could still see."

She looks up.

"So that is the long and the short of it."

* "You are not blaming him." -> blame
* "What do you want to do?" -> do

== blame ==
"I am not absolving him either. I do not do that; it is not mine to hand out and he would not take it." Flat, and not unkind. "He heard a door and he made a call with the information he had, in a pass full of men who were hunting him. I have made that call. Everybody who has ever led anybody has made that call."

"The difference is that mine came out on the right side often enough that people call me captain now."

* "What do you want to do?" -> do

== do ==
"Where is he?"

"Thornden. Behind the smithy, under his own name."

"Then when this is finished, I am going to Thornden, and I am going to stand there, and then I am going to find his sister and tell her he was good at his work." She picks up what she was holding. "You are coming. Not as a penance. Because she should hear it from the two people who were nearest."

* [Sit back down.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_BranSerraTold); grant_xp(100); affinity(+10); affinity(TSC_Npc_Serra, +10)
